+<!-- Owner: src/core/types.ts (World.leadingSystemSegments), src/core/prefix.ts -->
+
+# World leading system segments
+
+An operator-managed extension may implement `leadingSystemSegments()` to supply static
+`PrefixSegment` values before the Persona's system segments. Worlds are ordered by id;
+each World's segment order and text are preserved. The hook is optional. Without it,
+prefix assembly is unchanged. A failure propagates instead of omitting the rules.
+
+This hook is evaluated only during prefix assembly, including preview and reload. It
+must not produce timestamps, retrieval results, or other changing context. Edits take
+effect on the next prefix rebuild. A fork inheriting the main context also inherits the
+rules in that snapshot. Unmounted or hidden Worlds do not contribute to runtime assembly.
+
+The host exports `WORLD_LEADING_SYSTEM_SEGMENTS` from `core/prefix.ts` so extensions
+requiring this hook can reject incompatible hosts. Rule management and storage belong to
+the extension; Core does not interpret the text or enforce its semantic instructions.
